        "Antoine Georges",
        "Dieter Vollhardt",
        "Gabriel Kotliar"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory supplied a general and tractable way to understand strong local correlations, transforming the study of correlated electrons.",
        "attribution": "The credited theorists made major, complementary contributions to formulating and developing the method.",
        "maturity": "It has been tested and extended over decades and remains a central tool in condensed matter physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The method has several important intellectual precursors and a broad community of later contributors."
