        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Topological insulators and the quantum spin Hall effect established a new organizing principle for electronic phases and stimulated a large body of research.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied key theoretical predictions, while Molenkamp's group demonstrated the quantum spin Hall effect experimentally.",
        "maturity": "The original phenomena are well established, though the wider program of topological materials continues to evolve.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The scope of a prize spanning theory, a specific experimental realization, and the wider topological insulator field requires careful definition."
        ]
      }
    },
